# RepoSpool selects committed Git source; ignored files remain available in GitHub.
# Keep architecture, Rust/Svelte implementation, important tests, CI, and design docs.
# Dependency resolutions are useful for reproducing builds but low-value for an
# agent's compact source context. They remain tracked in the repository.
/Cargo.lock
/flake.lock
/frontend/package-lock.json

# One-off bootstrap workflow and historical preview troubleshooting are
# accessible directly in GitHub, but not required for the architecture snapshot.
/.github/workflows/lockfiles.yml
/docs/PREVIEW.md

# Machine-local/build outputs if they ever become tracked.
**/node_modules/
**/target/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/result/
**/result-*/
**/.direnv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/coverage/
**/.cache/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.map
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
*.bak
*.orig
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Sensitive machine-specific settings must never enter a shared snapshot.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
